Pizza Advertisement Recreation Using HTML and CSS

INTODUCTION:

The Pizza Advertisement Recreation is a web development practice project created using **HTML and CSS**. The main purpose of this project is to recreate a pizza advertisement design as a webpage.

This project helped in understanding how HTML is used to create the structure of a webpage and how CSS is used to improve its appearance, spacing, colors, borders, sizing, and overall layout.

The webpage represents a fictional pizza shop called **“Pizza Delight”** and contains different sections such as a hero section, special offers, popular pizzas, and a footer.

OBJECTIVE:

The main objectives of this project are:

* To practice HTML structure and elements.
* To understand how CSS can be used to style a webpage.
* To recreate an advertisement design using code.
* To learn how images can be added to a webpage.
* To understand tables and their styling.
* To practice borders, spacing, colors, text sizes, and alignment.
* To understand the use of external CSS.
* To organize HTML and CSS files properly.
* To practice using Git and GitHub for project version control.

TECHNOLOGIES USED:

### HTML

HTML (**HyperText Markup Language**) is used to create the basic structure of the webpage.

Some HTML elements used in this project include:

* `<html>`
* `<head>`
* `<title>`
* `<body>`
* `<div>`
* `<p>`
* `<h2>`
* `<img>`
* `<table>`
* `<tr>`
* `<td>`
* `<b>`
* `<pre>`

### CSS

CSS (**Cascading Style Sheets**) is used to control the visual appearance of the webpage.

CSS is used for:

* Background colors
* Text colors
* Font sizes
* Spacing
* Borders
* Image sizes
* Alignment
* Hero section styling
* Buttons
* Footer styling

PROJECT STRUCTURE:

The project contains two main files:

```text
Pizza Advertisement
│
├── varshini.html
└── adv.css
```

### `varshini.html`

This file contains the **structure and content** of the pizza advertisement.

### `adv.css`

This file contains the **styling** used to make the advertisement visually attractive.

---

ADVERTISEMENT SECTION:

The webpage is divided into several sections.

### 5.1 Pizza Delight Header

The webpage starts with the name:

**PIZZA DELIGHT**

The two words are given different colors to make the shop name visually attractive.

A tagline is also displayed:

**Fresh. Hot. Delicious.**


### 5.2 Hero Section

The hero section is the main promotional area of the advertisement.

It contains:

* **Hot Pizza.**
* **Happy You!**
* A short description
* **ORDER NOW** button
* A large pizza image

The section uses a yellow/golden background to make it stand out from the rest of the page.

CSS positioning is used to place the pizza image on the right side while the promotional text appears on the left.


### 5.3 Special Offers

The next section is titled:

**Our Special Offers**

It contains three offers:

1. **25% OFF**
   On all Pizzas

2. **Free Drink**
   On orders above ₹499

3. **Free Delivery**
   On orders above ₹299

Each offer is placed inside its own box with a **dotted border**. Images are placed beside the offer information.

---

### 5.4 Popular Pizzas

The webpage also contains a section called:

**Our Popular Pizzas**

It displays three pizza options:

### Veggie Pizza

Fresh veggies & cheese
**₹249**

### Chicken Pizza

Grilled chicken & cheese
**₹299**

### Cheese Pizza

100% real cheese
**₹199**

Each pizza is displayed inside a separate dotted-border box containing the pizza image, name, description, and price.


### 5.5 Footer

A green footer section is added at the bottom of the advertisement.

It contains promotional text such as:

**Freshly Made. Deliciously Served.**

**Order your favorite pizza today!**

**Call us: 98765 43210**

The dark green background provides a clear ending to the advertisement.


## 6. CSS Styling

CSS was used to improve the appearance of the webpage.

Some of the important CSS properties used are:

### `background-color`

Used to change the background color.

```css
background-color: gold;
```

### `color`

Used to change text color.

```css
color: darkgreen;
```

### `font-size`

Used to control the size of text.

```css
font-size: 50px;
```

### `padding`

Used to create space inside an element.

```css
padding: 20px;
```

### `margin`

Used to create space outside an element.

```css
margin: 15px;
```

### `border`

Used to create the dotted boxes around offers and pizzas.

```css
border: 2px dotted brown;
```

### `width` and `height`

Used to control the size of sections and images.

USE OF EXTERNEL CSS:

Initially, some styles were written directly inside HTML using inline CSS.

Later, the styling was moved to an external CSS file:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="adv.css">
```

This makes the HTML cleaner and allows all the styling to be maintained in one CSS file.


IMAGES USED:

Different images are used to make the advertisement more realistic.

Images are included for:

* Main pizza
* Pizza slice
* Drink
* Delivery
* Veggie pizza
* Chicken pizza
* Cheese pizza

The `<img>` element is used to display these images.

Example:

```html
<img src="pizza.png">
```


GIT AND GITHUB:
Git was used to manage the project files and GitHub was used to store the project online.

The project was initialized as a Git repository and the HTML and CSS files were committed.

The main files committed were:

```text
varshini.html
adv.css
```

The project was then connected to the GitHub repository:

**HTML_CSS_PRACTICE-ADVERTISEMENT-**

This provides practice with basic version control and helps maintain the project online.


LEARNING OUTCOMES :

Through this project, I learned:

* How to create a webpage using HTML.
* How to structure different sections of a webpage.
* How to add and resize images.
* How to create tables and organize content.
* How to use CSS classes.
* How to use an external CSS file.
* How to style buttons and sections.
* How to create dotted borders.
* How to control margins and padding.
* How to position images.
* How to create a simple advertisement layout.
* How to initialize a Git repository.
* How to commit project files.
* How to connect a local project to GitHub.


CONCLUSIONS :
The **Pizza Advertisement Recreation** project was a useful hands-on exercise for learning the fundamentals of HTML and CSS. By recreating an advertisement, I was able to understand how webpage structure and styling work together.

The project also provided practical experience with images, tables, CSS properties, external stylesheets, layout design, and GitHub. This project can be further improved by adding responsive design, navigation, animations, interactive buttons, and JavaScript functionality.
